{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/276-introductions-and-greetings","id":276,"title":"Introductions and Greetings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-01T10:47:56-07:00","id":276,"title":"Introductions and Greetings","content":"Since we're on a new version of the forums, I thought it might be a nice thing to have a thread where people can introduce themselves and talk a little bit about their history with gaming in general and White Wolf/Onyx Path games in particular. Since I started this thread, I guess I'll go first. =)<br /> <br /> My name is Jeremy, and I've been gaming since I was 13--about 20 years now. I started with GURPS and moved on to D&amp;D as my third or fourth game. My first exposure to the World of Darkness was in high school, but I didn't really get into White Wolf stuff until college, where I helped set up and manage a Vampire LARP that lasted about two years. I have a love/hate relationship with the Storyteller system; I love the settings, but I've never been able to run a tabletop game that lasted more than five sessions. XD<br /> <br /> My particular love is Exalted. Though I'm not that fond of the 2E system, I have a nearly complete collection of EX2 and I was a backer for EX3. I've been running an Exalted game for the last two years using Mutants &amp; Masterminds. We have an <a href=\"http://www.obsidianportal.com/campaigns/exalted-the-sun-also-rises\" target=\"_blank\">Obsidian Path wiki if anyone wants to see what we've done with the game</a>. I'm really looking forward to the new edition; maybe I'll actually get to run Exalted using the base system this time around.<br /> <br /> I was the user hidajiremi on the old forums; blackwingedheaven is what I use on most other forums, though, so I'm switching to it here.<br /> <br /> I've written for a few role-playing games, and I'm technically still a freelancer even though I haven't done much work lately. Graduate school don'tchaknow. In a few months, I'll have a master's degree in library and information science, and I'm already a card-carrying member of the ALA. I also write fiction, and I'm currently working on my first novel, <i>Seven Bridges</i>, in addition to writing a scandalous amount of Skyrim fanfiction.<br /> <br /> Hi, everyone! Let's make the new forums awesome! ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />&quot;The true object of all human life is play. Earth is a task garden; heaven is a playground.&quot; -G.K. Chesterton","edited":{"userid":53,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/53-blackwingedheaven","user":"blackwingedheaven","date":". 11-01-2013, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/53-blackwingedheaven","name":"blackwingedheaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar53_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T11:03:07-07:00","id":291,"title":"","content":"My name is <i>also Jeremy!</i><br /> <br /> I've been playing <i>White Wolf/Onyx Path</i> titles for long enough that I can count their presence in over half the years I've lived. Everything from <i>World of Darkness</i> to <i>Trinity Continuum</i> to that awesome few years when <i>Ravenloft</i> was in <i>Arthaus</i> hands.<br /> <br /> My particular loves are, in no particular order, both flavors of <i>Werewolf</i>, <i>Exalted</i>, <i>Trinity, Demon: the Fallen, </i>and now <i>Demon: the Descent</i>. <i>Changeling: the Dreaming</i> too, but that's a <i>secret.</i><br /> <br /> Other than that, I'm a filthy quote-unquote story gamer. Indie titles the likes of <i>Monsterhearts</i> and <i>Smallville</i> and <i>Dresden</i> have influenced how I approach the storyteller system.<br /> <br /> When I'm not playing make-believe, I'm a designer for an alternative energy company, and I doodle <i>like whoa</i>. Got a bit of graphic design under by belt. I love cats. And sriracha. Horror movies! I'd kill for a good <i>backrub.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17-metrophelean","name":"Metrophelean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T12:34:55-07:00","id":362,"title":"","content":"Well I'm kinda a new lurker, but my name is Cameron. I haven't been playing Games more than a year or so (Bloody near impossible for me to find groups). White wolf has always been my first love in Tabletop games ever since I found a second edition VtM at a garage sale. Though I love all the works in general, my personal favorites are Scion, Exalted, Old and new Demon, Mummy the Curse (even if I haven't played it yet, and both Vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/89-quatren","name":"Quatren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T13:09:34-07:00","id":403,"title":"","content":"I'm Rose. I've been a <i>Vampire</i> fan pretty much forever, and I joined White Wolf as a full-timer many years ago. I moved over to Onyx Path when CCP scaled back. Currently, I work on <i>Vampire</i>, <i>Demon</i>, and my creator-owned Onyx Path project <i>Cavaliers of Mars</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 11-01-2013, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T13:20:33-07:00","id":422,"title":"","content":"I'm Claire. I freakin' love World of Darkness games and have since I was barely reaching double-digits in age. Getting the opportunity to work on these games with some of the best people in this industry is a dream come true.<br /> <br /> Also, I wanna be a mod here. And how do you get longer signatures? I can't seem to get those!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T13:37:19-07:00","id":439,"title":"","content":"Claire - press enter in your sig box. It's formatable like any other text.<br /> <br /> I'm Dave. I've been lurking around White Wolf / Onyx Path since the early days - when the Web was newborn, I was dialing up Mage: The Ascension sites on an Acorn Archimedes. I was an Ascension fanboy, then an Awakening fan, then an Awakening freelancer, and about a year ago talked myself into being Awakening's Developer. Which has been a terrifying yet rewarding experience so far, and looks to be just as exciting over the next year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T14:03:54-07:00","id":462,"title":"","content":"I'm Stew. I've been playing RPGs since I was about 12, so twenty years this year. I hadn't even realised that until I typed this.<br /> <br /> I cut my teeth on <i>Werewolf</i>, ran a metafictional <i>Mage </i>game that we still talk about over whisky, and played for far too long in the old, old unmoderated White Wolf chats before New Bremen ever existed. I wrote a bit for the <i>Wraith Project</i> and for the<i> Trinity Storyteller's Handbook</i> before Ethan finally caved in and gave me a shot on <i>Lore of the Forsaken</i>. I went on to write a lot of <i>Forsaken</i>, a lot of <i>Hunter</i> (only one book without my name on it), a lot of <i>Geist</i>, a bunch of self-published indie games, then we brought back the classic World of Darkness. After W20, I got handed developership of <i>Werewolf: The Apocalypse</i>, then and talked my way into <i>Werewolf: The Forsaken</i> as well.<br /> <br /> It's been a crazy ride, and it's only getting warmed up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":28,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","user":"DigitalRaven","date":".  Fixed formatting 11-01-2013, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T14:10:41-07:00","id":472,"title":"","content":"I'm Chris, been gaming for something like 18 years.<br /> <br /> Currently working in Germany, doing my 2nd postdoc position in Theoretical Chemistry. I've in the past worked as a sales assistant for Games Workshop. I am also one of the hosts for Darker Days Radio. <a href=\"https://www.darker-days.org\" target=\"_blank\">www.darker-days.org</a> - a podcast devoted to New and Classic World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> My main loves are New World of Darkness, and right now I am gearing up for running Geist.<br /> <br /> Hopefully might be doing some more freelance writing in the near future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.darker-days.org\" target=\"_blank\">www.darker-days.org</a> - The Premier World of Darkness Podcast<br /> Co-designer and miniature painter for Noble Armada 3e<br /> Staff writer for CYBR Magazine <a href=\"https://shop.cybrmagazine.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://shop.cybrmagazine.com/</a><br /> Writer, developer, editor, layout for Darker Days Radio Publishing<br /> Writer for Cubicle 7 Wrath and Glory Revised","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/128-dr-ether","name":"Dr Ether","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar128_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T14:21:27-07:00","id":482,"title":"","content":"I'm Jaded, been for a while over the years on the old WW forums then I had to deal with medical problems. My ex also sold my WW collection behind my back for drugs (he is rotting now). I came back to get into the action and start writing again. My favorite characters are mainly Malkies due to personal experience. Studying V:tR right now but plan to get V20 after the first of the year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T14:24:15-07:00","id":488,"title":"","content":"I would be Matthew, known on YouTube as The Gentleman Gamer.<br /> <br /> I've been a fan and Storyteller of World of Darkness games since starting to role-play just over ten years ago, with the only games I've not played in or run to date being Changeling: The Dreaming and Mage: The Awakening. I hope to one day rectify this.<br /> <br /> I currently find myself split between the creation of videos that I use to promote the game line that I most love (being Vampire: The Masquerade) and my full-time job. I'm also assisting in development of the Book of the Wyrm 20th Anniversary Edition and am oft told that I have a passing resemblance to Harold Zettler, Pentex Director.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T16:43:52-07:00","id":685,"title":"","content":"I'm Amy. My first exposure to the White Wolf pathogen was through Mage: The Ascension, but I didn't really play anything else and stopped when Time of Judgment happened. I got back in through Changeling: The Lost and, god forgive me, Changing Breeds. Then Scion, Exalted, and Trinity over the course of the last six years. Right now I'm playing VtR and Aberrant, with plans for Exalted and Demon in the near future. So that's neat.<br /> <br /> I'm a writer and I get to actually write for Onyx Path how awesome is that?!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I had a signature but now I don't but it won't let me leave this blank so yeah.</b>","edited":{"userid":199,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/199-yue","user":"Yue","date":".  Butts! 08-15-2014, 06:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/199-yue","name":"Yue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar199_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T16:56:21-07:00","id":698,"title":"","content":"Another Matthew here, I've been into Gaming and White Wolf since my sophomore year of high school when my Math teacher (a Jesuit Priest) handed me a copy of V:tM revised. That was 12 years ago (Time flies when you're trying to figure out how Temporis works). I've run games of V:tM, V:tR, C:tL, H:tV, D:tF, nWoD mortals and (my personal favorite) Orpheus. Gearing up to play D:tF and V:tR. Everyone I game with fits the negative player type described in the Vampire Storytellers guide as &quot;The Loathsome Quoter&quot;, myself included.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/200-totalworlddomination","name":"TotalWorldDomination","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T17:07:47-07:00","id":706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/276-introductions-and-greetings?p=685#post685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm Amy. Much as I hate to admit it my first exposure to White Wolf was through Changeling: The Lost and, god forgive me, Changing Breeds. Then Scion, Exalted, and Trinity over the course of the last six years. Right now I'm playing VtR and Aberrant, with plans for Exalted and Demon in the near future. So that's neat.<br /> <br /> I'm a writer and spend much of my free time begging the OPP crew to let me help them with awesome stuff. So far, not so lucky.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling the Lost and Changing Breeds! You started with one of the best and one of the worst, how curious <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Back on-topic:<br /> <br /> I started with White Wolf games with Vampire: the Masquerade, never played anything else back in the day although I got curious about Mage: the Ascension but it blew my mind anytime I tried to read about it.<br /> <br /> Then came Requiem and the New WoD and although I got confused at first (most people thought it was some sort of post-Gehena setting) but I grew to like it as much or even more as it predecesor.<br /> <br /> And then it came the Crown Jewel and my all time favourite: Mage: the Awakening <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T17:40:14-07:00","id":733,"title":"","content":"Hello, I'm Craig Oxbrow. Yes, that really is my last name.<br /> <br /> Been a fan since, ohhh, the preview booklet for <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b> first edition. Now working on something which I can hopefully talk more about soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T17:49:45-07:00","id":738,"title":"","content":"Hoi, chummers. I'm Chris. My first exposure to White Wolf was through Trinity (somewhere I still have my copy of the original quickstart). Hell, my first exposure to non-D&amp;D games was through Trinity.<br /> <br /> My presence on various White Wolf-related fora go back to... oh, hell, long long ways. Back when guessing what the new MFP acronym meant was a good way to kill a few minutes. Good times. I've used this handle, or some variation on it, just about everywhere I've frequented online since 1998 or so (although I'm told there's some Malifaux player who calls himself that as well but so far that's only been confusing on Twitter and at a Netrunner tournament at Gencon this year).<br /> <br /> I've played several WoD (both WoDs) games over the years, mostly through medium-to-small LARPs simply because that's how the local gaming community tends to keep in touch. I've also run or helped run my share, and although once upon a time I swore never to do so again I'm actually planning on starting up a fresh one sometime after New Year's. It's either going to be Demon: The Descent or Requiem with the Blood and Smoke rules; haven't yet decided, but I'm looking forward to both books coming out regardless.<br /> <br /> And I've managed to get in a bit of freelance work, contributing to <b>Night Horrors: The Unbidden</b> and the upcoming <b>Rage Across the World</b> (and also stuff I probably shouldn't discuss publicly yet).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T18:41:18-07:00","id":763,"title":"","content":"Well then. A new start.<br /> Better introduce myself this time around.<br /> Hi, I'm Soren. I'm one of those weird Scandinavians types, more precisely, a Dane.<br /> Now, a bit of background.<br /> I've been a part of this hobby since late '99, as that was when this young impressionable soul picked up a copy of &quot;<b>LA by Night</b>&quot; and &quot;<b>A World of Darkness 2nd</b>&quot; at the local library. After that, it was a swift decent into the rest of the WOD, and a few years later, I discovered that you could actually play with other people, and soon, my social circle consisted mainly of the other role-players near me. I first joined up on the White Wolf forums under the nick &quot;<i>Dalerik</i>&quot;, way back in the days when we had all those jpeg images and there actually was a online community.<br /> After the Time of Judgement and the following reboot of the forums (I think mostly due to the bright colour-scheme), I left, and joined the Shadownessence fan forums as &quot;<i>Growls-at-the-Moon</i>&quot;, which was my nick as well when I rarely visited the WW boards, but in some great shuffle, my account was lost, but not my registrered e-mail, so I was left lurking for nearly 6 years, never bothering to call tech support.<br /> My interest in the WW games gradually waned, as fewer and fewer people I knew would play the WW games, and most of them had picked up either D&amp;D-clones or indie games. Then, I finally joined a game society who appriciated the WOD as much as I. Through them, I kept the OWoD/NWoD/Exalted flame alive in my heart, even as we sought new games.<br /> Cue V20, Onyx Path and the following products, and it lead me here, breathing in the spirit of the White Wolf.<br /> <br /> Aside from that?<br /> I'm a writer, having published a few articles and stories in my native language, I've been considering if my English vocabulary could be good enough for writing for a wider audience.<br /> I'm a LARPer, as it is actually bit of a national sport here in the DK, with thousands of kids having played boffer larps at one point or another. Personally, I'm a bit more into more serious affairs, as we actually have a fair share of WoD larps in Denmark, the oldest being a 15-year old Werewolf: The Apocalypse chronicle called &quot;<b>Rage Across Denmark</b>&quot;.<br /> Also a bit of a medieval re-enactment buff, mostly due to the shiny swords and armours.<br /> <br /> I run three campaigns at the moment:<br /> - &quot;<i>After Winter Follows Spring</i>&quot; a chronicle about a noble family, set in the &quot;Song of Ice &amp; Fire&quot;-universe, with intrigues, sex, honor and backstabbing.<br /> - &quot;<i>Silk &amp; Steel</i>&quot;, a Legend of the Five Rings campaign about a empire recovering from a civil war, with five young samurai making their way in the world.<br /> (I've actually put up a Actual Play thread of this up on RPG.Net, poke me for more info)<br /> - &quot;<i>Vampires of the Caribbean</i>&quot;, A Vampire20 chronicle set in the british colony of Jamaica, in the year 1660, with the Sabbat and the Camarilla vying for control over the New World, with a trio of vampires having barely escaped the Inquisition, finds themselves shipwrecked and 150 years out of time, and worst of all, only to find the Jyhad has found them already.<br /> <br /> On the more boring side?<br /> I work for a Computer Stress Test company and does a bit of transcribing of medical journals for a local doctor. It pays the bills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T18:50:42-07:00","id":768,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">Hello, I'm Kismet, and I was introduced to tabletop roleplaying games through Vampire: the Masquerade in October of 1995 by the guy I'm privileged to be living with now. Then, a couple years ago I wooed him to the nWoD and we've been happily doing what we want with the old and new systems ever since. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I started a web site for Vampire a few years later and have kept it going, including material for the nWoD (<a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/</a>) in what little free time I've had. I got to really play and run V:tDA and W:tA, although I read a number of the oWoD games and I wasn't done with the old game when the new system rolled out. I admit that I wasn't fully sold on the nWoD until I got my eager paws on Changeling: the Lost, although I did love the nWoD's focus on mortals and a return to mystery. In the end, the stability of the system finally won me over. The flexibility of the system has held me, and recent releases like Mummy: the Curse and Demon have had me looking forward to more.<br /> <br /> I have a strange, obsessive love for Damnation City that I've never been able to get out of my system, and aside from many of the Changeling books, it's one of my favorite releases. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T18:56:11-07:00","id":772,"title":"","content":"I'm Daydreamer. I used to post on the old forums, from time to time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T19:11:32-07:00","id":780,"title":"","content":"My name is Shan..been a member since..1st Ed Masquerade. Occasional lurker, occasional poster, occasional person who calls for calm when the forums seem to be heating up. <br /> <br /> My favorite games in order: <br /> <br /> Mage: The Ascension/Exalted (All Editions of both) <br /> Werewolf: The Apocalypse (All Editions of both)<br /> The Aeon-Verse (cept the d20 stuff..it buuurns) <br /> Vampire the Masq. (All editions)<br /> Werewolf: The Forsaken<br /> Wraith/Changeling the Lost.(Damned ties) <br /> the rest of oWoD/NWoD<br /> <br /> I can't wait to see what other wonderful stuff you guys come up with. <br /> <br /> Good Luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/238-hammerofheaven","name":"HammerofHeaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar238_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T19:27:21-07:00","id":798,"title":"","content":"nicodemus, checking in and trying the new forum. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> been with WW since '95. cut my teeth on Masquerade. ran a LARP for a couple of years, and a Kindred of the East game for 4 years and 5 chronicles. that was my best. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> now i'm finally jumping into nWoD with Mummy: the Curse and loving it. prepping to run my second session as i type this.<br /> <br /> keep gaming, all!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZinR2EXjdSmNAlIoj0eVUtNW61dvSgz-45XyKTOQt4g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">VtR 2v5 Homebrew: VtR 2e base with my favorite V5 mechanics</a>","edited":{"userid":241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","user":"nicodemus","date":". 11-01-2013, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","name":"nicodemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T19:59:24-07:00","id":826,"title":"","content":"Hey, I'm Zach. My first soiree into WoD was playing the Masquerade RPG on the computer and put more hours than I'd care to admit into it and after that I found a book called Hunger Like Fire at a garage sale. I guess you could say that was the final nail in the coffin so to speak, once I finished that book I bought VtR, VtM and got my friend into the game. Since then, both of us own all the splats and to this day we still bounce character ideas off of each other. Even though I'm pretty new to the community with only about 2 and half years under my belt, I'll hope to be a part of WoD (and Scion!) for as long as physically possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T20:29:05-07:00","id":852,"title":"","content":"I'm Telgar, and I've been playing RPG's (mostly Vampire, Exalted and Scion) since 1999. I'm 26, and I'm a professor of photography. I'm really looking forward to DAV20, Wraith20, Trinity Continuum, Scion2 and Exalted3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T20:50:52-07:00","id":875,"title":"","content":"I'm Jim. I enjoy White Wolf games but don't live near anyone who plays 'em, so my interest is mostly in the forum community, where I whine about feeling sad and people inexplicably thank me for it. I don't get it, but I've decided to let it ride.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T21:04:40-07:00","id":885,"title":"","content":"Hello friends, I'm Yani. After being invited to a session of <i>Vampire: The Requiem</i>, and then not being allowed to play due to the laziness of the Storyteller, I joined a session of <i>Changeling: The Lost</i>, and I found my new obsession. I have an undying fascination with the Changelings, the Fae, Arcadia itself.. all of it has just drawn me in for some reason and I don't feel like leaving yet. It's pretty much taken over my way of thinking, and I've been working for almost a month creating some homebrew Merits and a couple of likewise Contracts. I've made 17 playable Changelings, as well as 6 Fetch. I have an undying fascination with the Darkling Seeming, if it wasn't obvious enough. I'd love to say more, but I have to figure out where the heck my charge cord is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/268-darkling","name":"Darkling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T21:11:28-07:00","id":890,"title":"","content":"I'm Ian.<br /> <br /> First got involved in... 1995, 1996? Somewhere around there, when some gamer friends introduced me to Vampire once we'd wrapped up an AD&amp;D game. During a break in Planescape releases in 1996, I started snapping up rulebooks for all the game lines, with Vampire and Mage as my favourites to this day.<br /> <br /> In 1999 I got involved in the <i>Wolf Pack</i> demo team program, and shortly thereafter in 2000 I was one of the original ten Storytellers on the <i>New Bremen</i> moderated chats, spending a year as the Head Mage ST. It was in this guise that Jess Heinig approached me for my opinion on a number of items going into the <b>Guide to the Traditions</b>, making that my first RPG credit (albeit as &quot;additional contributions&quot;). I also helped jumpstart a number of the other chats, including the <i>Trinity/Aberrant</i> chat, <i>Fangsfall</i> (Scarred Lands), <i>Rookhausen</i> (Ravenloft), and <i>Jade City</i> (Exalted).<br /> <br /> In 2001 I started fansite <i>Wolfspoor</i>, which started off as a WW news and rumour site, but later evolved into just a host for my numerous avatars and icons. In 2002/2003, I got together a bunch of fans to make a <b>Trinity Storytellers Handbook</b>. The project was never completed, but I'm really proud of the work that was done.<br /> <br /> In 2004 I got my first published work in Scarred Lands' <b>Edge of Infinity: The Scarred Planes</b>. I also started up the <i>Unofficial White Wolf Wiki</i>, which continues to this day.<br /> <br /> Since then I've had my finger in a bunch of pies. Graphics, chat site coding, videos, and so on. In early 2012, Rich asked me to be lead developer on the new Trinity Continuum. Later, after asking my opinion on what sort of thing should appear on the new Onyx Path website, given my experience building and running fansites, and my awareness of the requirements on a business end as well as the fan side of things, Eddy uttered the fatal words: &quot;why don't we just get Ian to do the website?&quot;<br /> <br /> That takes us to today, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T21:32:58-07:00","id":899,"title":"","content":"I'm Trym. I am Norwegian. I've been playing roleplaying games since I was eleven, thanks to my dad. I realize that I was kind of doomed from the start thanks to him. I study english in Bergen, Norway and host a show for a local radio station. I was always interested in Vampire as a gameline (Thanks to the CCG Vampire: The Eternal Struggle, or Jyhad), but missed out on The Masquerade. So, I picked up nWoD at one point. I now own most of the gamelines (except for Mummy), with my favorite being Promethean. I've even gotten my claws on some of the older WoD titles like Orpheus, Wraith and Demon. I currently play in a fairly irregular Hunter: The Vigil game. It's fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/273-morte","name":"Morte","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar273_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T22:12:10-07:00","id":908,"title":"","content":"I'm Hilary, I am a class act and a people person. I like reading and running. Rap is my favorite music. I got into rpgs a year or two ago and I like pretty much all of the nwod gamelines except for Mage and Werewolf (nothing against them, just never clicked), although I mostly play apocalypse world and some of the hacks. Demon looks cool. So do these new forums. Thanks for doing them, Onyx Path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T22:36:45-07:00","id":913,"title":"","content":"I'm Alex, and I'm here for the Exalted ethical discussions. I also enjoyed Vampire: Bloodlines and am vaguely aware of oWoD Mage via the official GURPS conversion. I've been running D&amp;D since '08 since I can't get anyone to play anything else most of the time. I did run a year-long second edition Exalted Skype game, after which I swore to never actually play it ever again. I tend to gush about Exalted's hell, but regardless of what anyone might say, I did not have sexual relations with the Green Sun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm working on it, all right?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/130-gensh","name":"Gensh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar130_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T03:02:22-07:00","id":1013,"title":"","content":"Hi. I'm Dean. My interest in (and awareness of) roleplaying games started with TSR's Endless Quest books and the advertisement for Dungeons and Dragons in the back (and the red box D&amp;D set being my first roleplaying game) nearly 30 years ago.<br /> <br /> The Internets wasn't popular back in the day when Vampire: The Masquerade was first publish so only came to my attention when a fellow Uni Student brought a copy of the 1st Ed. into the Uni Game Club. That lead to me purchasing Werewolf and V:TM 2nd Edition. But Mage was the first World of Darkness game that really pulled me in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is a signature &lt;-----------","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/118-shining-dragon","name":"Shining Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T04:10:44-07:00","id":1044,"title":"","content":"My friends call me Murphy. I took this screen name on the old forums because murphy was taken and I couldn't think of anything else, and kept it on the off chance someone remembered me. I've been playing since the D&amp;D red box, and now I have a giant stack of Requiem books and no one to share with. But I still love the forums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T06:20:01-07:00","id":1077,"title":"","content":"My name is Weimann, I got into White Wolf through Exalted at some point in 2009 or early 2010, and I've promptly stayed there. I don't play much, but I like reading and talking about the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T10:36:04-07:00","id":1151,"title":"","content":"Hi, I'm Peter. I'm a Swedish gamer who got into Vampire the Masquerade back in 2000, and never looked back. I've been around the White-Wolf boards in several different incarnations, from Curry Shrimp, to Pork Sword, back to my original forum handle from back in the day: Infernal Goose.<br /> <br /> I'm an avid fan of both incarnations of the World of Darkness and most of my interaction with the games manifests itself through pbp-games. If you're interested in finding a good pbp-portal, I'd recommend checking out the Malkavian Madness Forums, where I can be found posting under the Kapten handle. <br /> <br /> I've also played a lot of VtES back in the day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">Malkavian Madness Forum</a> - Your pbp fix. Be it nWoD, cWoD, CoC, D&amp;D or something else entirely, come over here and get your game on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/348-infernalgoose","name":"InfernalGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T12:12:43-07:00","id":1202,"title":"","content":"Hey all. JT are my initials, so almost my name. <br /> <br /> Was Charles Altmont (ITX NPC in my first Mage game and not even remotely like my real name) and then MasterKitsune on the original boards back in dark age knows as &quot;the 1990s.&quot; Currently TechnocratJT on most message boards or online fora. Perfectly happy to join up once again, and hello to those from the before time as well as other current places.<br /> <br /> Trying to decide how best to control my professional wall as I focus on my own little shingle aimed at geek legal needs and my current sig is a bit of a compromise that might soon be moot. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>J. T. Legal</b><br /> The other kind of rules lawyer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/334-technocratjt","name":"TechnocratJT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar334_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T13:56:32-07:00","id":1276,"title":"","content":"Hi<br /> I'm from Israel don\u2019t really play any more just collecting<br /> I have been posting on and off since the forum was neon green (mostly in the off topic section)<br /> Maybe ill post more this time around will see <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;and what is the use of a book&quot;, thought Alice, &quot;without pictures or conversations?&quot;<br /> - Lewis Carroll, Alice in Wonderland","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/395-almoni","name":"Almoni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar395_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T14:05:04-07:00","id":1286,"title":"","content":"[Salutatory phrase]. I'm Kevin, better (and preferentially) known by my username and still getting used to the notion that I somehow have a reputation on the old forums.<br /> <br /> I've been actively consuming TTRPG material for a relatively short time compared to most other people here; coming up on four or five years now, with most of that being nWoD and a smattering of Exalted 2e, though my passive intake of the material goes back a few more years, courtesy of a Let's Play of Bloodlines and a good friend who was a fan of oWoD.<br /> <br /> I'm a bit of a recovering lurker and consequent tone-police; people not understanding when their opinions aren't relevant, or failing to recognize how to present those opinions without sounding <i>\u2026needlessly unpleasant</i> is a bit of a bugbear of mine.<br /> <br /> I'm also presently in the process of reading closely and thoroughly through as much of the nWoD as I can to feed my burgeoning cosmology/metaphysics/lore-hunger, having gotten most of my initial understanding through skimming everything that wasn't a character-creation chapter; I'm about halfway through Werewolf with plans to work by way through the rest of the lines in rough order of book-count. The last stretches of college, the first legs of job-hunting, and the incoming new material may put a dent in my rate of consumption over the winter, but that's largely academic at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-02-2013, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T15:00:50-07:00","id":1318,"title":"","content":"Greeting and salutations! <br /> <br /> <br /> You can call me Joey, if you dig first names and that kinda junk. I prefer Azrael, if I'm not familiar with ya, but that's just a preference.<br /> <br /> WoD fan since Kindred was on tv and player/ST since late '99<br /> <br /> I mostly play Vampire (cWod, nWoD), Mage (both) and Werewolf: the Apocalypse, but I'm always expanding my WoD library and gaming experiences..<br /> <br /> Just got HtV and Slashers, if anyone wants to geek-out on them with me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I make a lot of Homebrew stuff for WoD, which I sometimes posted on the WW forums and will likely continue to do so here.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T15:02:18-07:00","id":1319,"title":"","content":"holla<br /> i'm eric annnddd i'm pretty into tabletop stuff, but i'm still relatively new to it all. i've been playing for something like..3 years now, i think? started off with vampire: the masquerade, which i've been playing pretty consistently until just this year. i've played some D&amp;D, i've played WH40k Inquisitor, Deathwatch..gotten a taste of a lot of different tabletop systems, i guess.<br /> <br /> my biggest interests probably lie in exalted and vtm, and i guess i'd just kind of like to interact and get more into the white wolf related tabletop community, since my experiences with tabletop gaming has generally been condensed to a ..fairly small group of people and it's always nice to branch out and actually start talking with people about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2649","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/403-mabufufu","name":"mabufufu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar403_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T19:54:29-07:00","id":1457,"title":"","content":"Hey folks<br /> <br /> I'm Chris, being the big Trinity goober that I am I setup and ran Aeon fansite EurOpNet ('EON') many years ago, the content of which eventually found its way over to rpgpost long after I moved on.<br /> <br /> I've been gaming for 25 or so years, starting with 2nd Ed AD&amp;D way back. My bookshelves strain from the number of systems I've collected (literally hundreds), but my faves are Trinity (duh), Cthulhu, Dune, Pendragon, Paranoia, Dark Heresy, Shadowrun, and I have a soft spot for old DnD properties like the Realms &amp; Dark Sun.<br /> <br /> I'm lucky enough to have tracked down and bought some of the original Trinity art from people like Leif Jones, including things like the Strike Team Psion drawing among others. Those bad boys all now hang in my crowded office / gaming room. Otha watches over me as I work, its a little freaky. <br /> <br /> Yes, a Trinity kickstarter will likely bankrupt me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T08:58:24-08:00","id":1818,"title":"","content":"I'm Chris. Been a fan and player of White Wolf products since 2000. While I prefer the CWoD I do enjoy the NWoD and I've been slowly getting into Exalted (backed the 3rd Ed KS so waiting for that before I really get into it).<br /> <br /> Favorite CWoD lines:<br /> Mage: the Ascension and its historical setting games. I'm a proud Daedalean and Technocrat.<br /> Vampire: the Masquerade, my first White Wolf game and RPG so it holds a special place in my heart.<br /> Hunter: the Reckoning, I've always loved the desperate and frantic nature of the game.<br /> Wraith: the Oblivion and Orpheus, two gamelines people tend to pass up or ignore, usually because of its subject matter but both lines are well worth checking out.<br /> Werewolf: the Apocalypse<br /> <br /> Currently reading:<br /> Mummy: the Curse and Kindred of the East, bought the PDFs for my birthday not too long ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T09:59:31-08:00","id":1853,"title":"","content":"hello, my name is Ignacio, from Argentina and i like whores <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>*</b></span></span><br /> <br /> Started RP when i was 15 i think, being doing it for almost 10 years now. Started with a very unusual DM of D&amp;D, then went on with NWoD with VtR wich never clicked for myself. The MtAw whom i have i love/hate relationship (i see the potential of what it could be but it isnt), then WtF wich was my absolute favorite game of the NWoD lines and Changeling wich i like but i cant find players to run it with.<br /> After NWoD i dabble with Deadlands (wich i love) and Dresden Files RPG (wich has nice ideas but didnt click with me).<br /> Then i gave Shadowrun a chance and found out that i love it and it has become the standar by wich i compare other RPGs and this leap of faith with Shadowrun allow me to give a chance to the OWoD line (wich the players of my country have left me with a very bad impression) and found out i love VtM and MtAs is awesome as a game while i havent yet decided on WtA.<br /> <br /> As my signature says i like the setting of WoD (both New and Old) but dont really care that much for the &quot;personal Horror&quot; theme of it. As contrary to what i led on i have had good players in my games but bad player IMO are the ones worth mentioning and &quot;fixing&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">*</span></b>high internet five for those who understand that reference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","user":"kaho","date":". 11-03-2013, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T11:06:15-08:00","id":1885,"title":"","content":"Hi, my name is Murray, and I've been a World of Darkness gamer since... when did Mage 1st come out again?<br /> <br /> Back in the last century I used to hang around the old Java Chat running by the handle &quot;Allamistako&quot;. Dropped out of the World of Darkness just after the revised editions were released, and sold off everything except a few Mage and Wraith books, and regret that terribly now. Got back in with &quot;the other Mage&quot; when it was released, but have now returned to the classic World of Darkness (Thanks in great part to my girlfriend who runs one of the two local Masquade LARP groups). Favorite cWoD games are M:tA, W:tO and V:tDA, nWoD games would be C:tL and RfR.Apart from that I'm a big fan of Scion and have recently discovered the Aeonverse. A brit living in Germany, I was also part of the team that translated Hunter to german. Please don't hit me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/373-infernal-teddy","name":"Infernal Teddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar373_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T11:20:56-08:00","id":1890,"title":"","content":"Heyyo, you can call me Witch, and I got into this mess around 2009 when I stumbled across a PBP game of <i>Werewolf: the Forsaken.</i> I didn't get to play much, but I've been hooked ever since. Other lines I enjoy are <i>Innocents,</i> <i>Hunter: the Vigil, Promethean</i>, and <i>Changeling: the Lost.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/542-witch","name":"Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T15:38:03-08:00","id":2111,"title":"","content":"Hullo, I'm Ed, a graduate Geneticist, and I've been gaming ever since a mate of mine bought the VtR core for curiosity's sake. Next spawned a short game where we burned through Chicago, setting fire to an airport and joining VII. I &quot;think&quot; I've calmed down since.<br /> <br /> The first game I ST'd was WtF, and it has been my passion ever since, I'm kinda looking forward to the Idigam Chronicles. I love Mage the Awakening, having run that at my university. Recently I've played a religious murder hobo in VtR, so I am pretty stoked for Blood and Smoke.<br /> <br /> That's it I suppose. Oh, I'm not a duck by the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T00:49:22-08:00","id":2467,"title":"","content":"I'm Leath - I've lurked around the old WW forums for quite a while. I first played 1st ed VtM in... '93 (owned it for a year or two before that), and from there fell in love with WtA and the others. I resisted the move into nWoD for a few years, because I was convinced that I didn't need any more books on the WoD. CtL changed all that and dragged me back in. My wallet still hasn't forgiven me, but those books look so pretty lined up on the shelves. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I've written bits and pieces for other game lines in the past, but hadn't done any for some time. Through a random confluence of events I was recently asked to help out writing some of the stretch goals for CB20. Now that I've had that taste I hope the various devs will keep me in mind for more. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T01:25:55-08:00","id":2475,"title":"","content":"Hello, my name is The Revenge of TV Head. You killed my father. Prepare to die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T06:23:13-08:00","id":2554,"title":"","content":"Hi my name is Joe. I have 3 dogs and am getting married to my partner of 7 years in the spring (he proposed for my birthday) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Ive been a fan of World of Darkness since 1997, started with Vampire the Masquerade then jumped onto Werewolf the Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> 3 years ago Drumheller (Louis Garcia) tapped me to join Dead Gamers Society, an amazing group of dedicated WOD gamers, and Ive been active in that meet-up as one of its organizers.<br /> <br /> I've gamed with Kismetrose, who manages some amazing WOD themed Facebook groups, and have been happy to be part of this community (in its various iterations) for a long while. <br /> <br /> Im currently storytelling Vampire the Requiem and Mummy the Curse for Dead Gamers Society. We meet at Cal State Fullerton university (OC) and in my neigbhorhood in Los Angeles. Recently, I got to meet some of you in person at Los Angeles By Night, where DGS partnered up with Dave Martin and his awesome Wrecking Crew. All in all I am very happy to be part of such a great group of gamers.<br /> <br /> I hope to continue my love for WOD and to make new friendships here.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T07:10:12-08:00","id":2584,"title":"","content":"Hi, I'm Gr\u00e9goire. I write stuff sometimes.<br /> <br /> I'm here because VtM: Bloodlines is the best game ever and strings of happenstance led me to think Exalted is freaking awesome. Also Vampire. Also Changeling.<br /> <br /> I met the best people ever on the precursors of this forum, and I hope I'll keep meeting and talking to awesome people on these.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T07:44:16-08:00","id":2611,"title":"","content":"Hey, for security reasons, I have to keep it to Papa Bear, often shorted to P Bear, &quot;Da Bears&quot; (with Chicago accent) is also acceptable, native Coloradan (for those of you outside the US, that's one of those little subsections of &quot;Crazy Americans&quot;). I've been interested in gaming since before there was White Wolf, and stumbled into Vampire: the Masquerade around 1993 or 1994 (I forget exactly). Classic WOD, I was my group's &quot;go-to&quot; on <b>Mage: the Ascension</b>, <b>Wraith: the Oblivion </b>and <b>Hunter: the Reckoning</b> and the designated ST for the latter half of that group's existence. For New WOD, I've had very little opportunity to run/play, but I tend to h(a)unt the <b>Werewolf: the Forsaken</b> forums more than any other line, and usually spend more time in the Off-Topic section than anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T07:55:24-08:00","id":2618,"title":"","content":"Hey all, I'm Jay, as my username suggests, I did go by the name Malkavian on the old forums but I haven't posted there in years I'm afraid, so this gives me a fresh start in order to get back into the old forums again.<br /> <br /> I'm 25 and I'm from Liverpool, United Kingdom. I started playing RPG's with Vampire the Masquerade in 2007 or 8 and I've been in love with White Wolf ever since, to the point I was in a Masuerade LARP for 4 years. - My favourite White Wolf game line has to be Changeling: The Lost.<br /> <br /> Outside of tabletop gaming my hobbies include writing, playing the guitar/ukulele, and collecting retro video games. I'm also a small time hockey fan. <br /> I look forward to meeting you all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/652-jay-stewart","name":"Jay Stewart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar652_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T09:19:00-08:00","id":2675,"title":"","content":"Here Stefano, from Italy<br /> I began rolpeplaying with &quot;The Ancestral Trail&quot; when I was about 10, following with &quot;Mutant Chronicles&quot; 1-2 years later (thanks for both to my grandpa).<br /> At 15, at a birthday-party, I was enrolled as NPC in a Vampire the Masquerade LARP (a Giovanni grunt, that actually managed to knock down the entire coterie of players <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). Since then, I began playing VampireTM and then storytelling it.<br /> Now, I'm storytelling a fourfold chronicle of VTM (maybe, this time, I'll manage to end it).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/276-introductions-and-greetings?p=685#post685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a writer and spend much of my free time begging the OPP crew to let me help them with awesome stuff. So far, not so lucky.</div> </div> </div> </div>same here, I keep harassing the OPP staff with my projects :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> 